<section class="section">
  <div class="container split split--reverse">
    <div class="split__media">{% image "/images/projects/bespoke-oak-desk/03.jpg", "Hand-cut dovetails on a drawer box in the workshop", "(min-width: 900px) 45vw, 100vw" %}</div>
    <div class="split__text prose">
      <h2 class="section-title">Working with one craftsman</h2>
      <p>Joel works on his own. The person who visits your home, designs and draws each piece, chooses the timber, makes it and fits it is the same person from start to finish, so you always know who to speak to, and the ideas agreed at the start are carried right through to the finished room.</p>
      <p>Working alone also means he takes on only a few projects at a time. Ask him why, and he will put it simply:</p>
      <figure class="pull-quote">
        <blockquote><p>“I'd rather take on fewer projects and give each one the time, care and attention it deserves.”</p></blockquote>
        <figcaption>Joel Dyter</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>After more than {{ site.yearsTrade }} years at the bench, very little about an old house surprises him. Uneven stone walls, sloping floors and openings that are nowhere near square are simply part of the job, and <strong><em>he takes the time to get them right</em></strong>. One client described how he “took great time to make sure everything was to my liking before taking the next step”.</p>
      <p>Joel would never say so himself, but his clients do. One wrote that “nothing prepared me for the professionalism and skill of the man”, and another that <strong><em>“his attention to detail is incredible and workmanship is of the very highest standard”</em></strong>.</p>
      <p>He uses the best timber and fittings he can source, because his work is meant to be lived with for a long time, and every piece of furniture leaves the workshop with his maker's plate. Many clients come back to him again and again. As one put it: “I've used Joel on many occasions over the last few years for kitchens, internal &amp; external doors, staircase and furniture … He is my first choice for quality cabinet making.”</p>
      <p>Whether you are thinking of a whole kitchen or a single bookcase, traditional or contemporary, Joel is always happy to talk it through.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--dark">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">The process</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">What to expect, start to finish</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><h3>Conversation</h3><p>Get in touch by phone, WhatsApp or the enquiry form to talk through what you have in mind.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Photos &amp; site visit</h3><p>A few photos give Joel a first idea of the room. He then visits to measure up and see how you use the space.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Estimate</h3><p>An early estimate gives you a sense of the cost before any detailed design work begins.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Drawings</h3><p>Joel draws up the design, so you can see how each piece will look and fit the room.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Final price &amp; agreement</h3><p>Once the design is settled, the build price is agreed. Changes requested mid-build, and the cost of fitting, may vary depending on the work involved.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Made by hand</h3><p>Cabinets and furniture are made by hand in the Hebden Bridge workshop.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Fitting</h3><p>Joel fits each piece himself, scribing it to your walls and floors so it sits neatly in the room.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <p class="steps__note">{{ site.bookingNote }}</p>
  </div>
</section>

